tore is also next to yet another  marijuana dispensary and then a  voiceover warns that there's just going  to be so many dispensaries that are  going to be selling edibles that look  like candy etc etc let's take a look at  the ad let's listen to the ad and as  ridiculous as the ad is what's even more  insane is who is funding this ad that  after we look at it question four would  allow thousands of pot shops and  marijuana operators throughout  Massachusetts in neighborhoods like  yours shops that sell pot edibles that  look like candy and high potency  marijuana in pro pot states incidents of  drugged driving and fatal car accidents  are on more pot shops and McDonald's and  Starbucks combined higher potency  dangerous drivers  it's the reason health professionals are  urging them to vote no on four think  about the sick irony here the group  behind the ad is the campaign for a safe  and healthy Massachusetts the group's  biggest donors come from the state's  largest distributors of alcohol wine and  spirit wholesalers of Massachusetts  incorporated and beer distributors of  Massachusetts incorporated gave  seventy-five thousand dollars to this  group a bunch of local bars donated  thousands more to oppose question for  the legalization of marijuana according  to the Massachusetts office of campaign  and political finance alcohol is  responsible for an insane number of  fatal car accidents and alcohol unlike  how marijuana would be if legalized  isn't sold only at alcohol only stores  you can get alcohol at supermarkets you  can get alcohol at convenience stores  and get it almost everywhere and edibles  look like candy you know there's a laugh  a lot of apple juice Pat that looks like  alcohol to me and it's being sold at  Whole Foods and this ads seems to  portray things that are just patently  false I mean I'm not gonna be able to  drive around smoking and the kid that  comes out at the end looks like he's  like 15 16 years old I mean this is some  real reefer